IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- PART 12ZD, STATUTORY PARENTAL BEREAVEMENT PAY, ss 171ZZ6 to 171ZZ15 (src:4017-4129).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively.  The source is a plain-text rendering made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
--
-- How to read a result (the rule of 2026-10-29):
--   JUST FALSE / JUST TRUE : the text says no / yes in its own words (each "no" branch quotes them).
--   NOTHING                : not covered (each branch says why: silent, list not closed, includes,
--                            undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording).
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Money is a NUMBER in pounds sterling.  Rates, periods and lengths that regulations supply are
-- INPUTS.  Dates are `Date day month year`.

§ `Part 12ZD -- Statutory parental bereavement pay`

§§ `s 171ZZ6 Entitlement`

-- Nouns.  The child who died, as a witness would state it.  For a stillborn child the "day the
-- child died" is the day of birth (s 171ZZ15(b)), so the birth day is always asked.
DECLARE `s 171ZZ6 the child who died` HAS
    `born dead`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `weeks of pregnancy when labour began` IS A NUMBER       -- read only when born dead
    `the day the child was born`           IS A DATE
    `the day the child died`               IS A MAYBE DATE   -- NOTHING for a stillborn child

-- The facts of the person's case that s 171ZZ6(2) reads.
DECLARE `s 171ZZ6(2) the person's case` HAS
    `the child who died`    IS A `s 171ZZ6 the child who died`
    `the employment`        IS AN Employment
    `weeks of continuous employment ending with the relevant week`                      IS A NUMBER
    `normal weekly earnings in pounds for the 8 weeks ending with the relevant week`    IS A NUMBER
    `at the end of the relevant week the person was entitled to be in that employment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person satisfies the prescribed conditions as to relationship with the child who died` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1) The grant.  "A person who satisfies the conditions in subsection (2) is entitled".
-- A failed "who satisfies" is counted as the text's no (reading (a), for a lawyer).
-- Regulations under s 171ZZ7(4) may modify or disapply conditions: if one does, the text alone cannot answer.
-- src:4019 | (1) A person who satisfies the conditions in subsection (2) is entitled in accordance with the following provisions of this Part to payments to be known as “statutory parental bereavement pay”.
@ref s 171ZZ6(1) (src:4019)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 171ZZ6(2) the person's case`
      `s 173(a) the person is under 18` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `WRA 2012 s 63(3) the day on which it comes fully into force` IS A DATE
      `s 171ZZ7(4) regulations modify or disapply a condition in the person's case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ6(1) the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay` MEANS
    IF `s 171ZZ7(4) regulations modify or disapply a condition in the person's case`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 171ZZ7(4)(a) and (c) let regulations modify the conditions or say that (2)(c) has no effect
    ELSE `s 171ZZ6(2) the person satisfies the conditions`
             facts
             `s 173(a) the person is under 18`
             `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds`
             `WRA 2012 s 63(3) the day on which it comes fully into force`

-- (2) The conditions.  All of (a) to (e).  A false paragraph makes the whole false (FALSE-kind:
-- "A person who satisfies the conditions in subsection (2) is entitled" -- reading (a));
-- paragraph (a) alone can be NOTHING (the child's status is not covered), so NOTHING only if every
-- other paragraph is satisfied.
-- src:4020 | (2) The conditions are—
-- src:4021 | (a) that the person is a bereaved parent,
-- src:4022 | (b) that the person has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks ending with the relevant week,
-- src:4023 | (c) that at the end of the relevant week the person was entitled to be in that employment (but see subsection (7)),
-- src:4024 | (d) that the person's normal weekly earnings for the period of 8 weeks ending with the relevant week are not less than the lower earnings limit in force under section 5(1)(a) at the end of the relevant week, and
-- src:4025 | (e) that the person has been in employed earner's employment with the employer by reference to whom the condition in paragraph (b) is satisfied for a continuous period beginning with the end of the relevant week and ending with the day on which the child dies.
@ref s 171ZZ6(2) (src:4020-4025)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 171ZZ6(2) the person's case`
      `s 173(a) the person is under 18` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `WRA 2012 s 63(3) the day on which it comes fully into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ6(2) the person satisfies the conditions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 171ZZ15(b) the day taken as the day the child dies`
                 (facts's `the child who died`'s `born dead`)
                 (facts's `the child who died`'s `the day the child was born`)
                 (facts's `the child who died`'s `the day the child died`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the day the child died is not given, so the relevant week and the end of the employment cannot be fixed
    WHEN JUST dies THEN
        IF NOT (    `s 171ZZ6(2)(b) the person has been in employment for at least 26 weeks`
                      (facts's `weeks of continuous employment ending with the relevant week`)
                AND `s 171ZZ6(2)(c) the person was entitled to be in that employment`
                      (facts's `at the end of the relevant week the person was entitled to be in that employment`)
                      (`s 171ZZ6(7) paragraph (c) of subsection (2) is omitted` dies `WRA 2012 s 63(3) the day on which it comes fully into force`)
                AND `s 171ZZ6(2)(d) the normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit`
                      (facts's `normal weekly earnings in pounds for the 8 weeks ending with the relevant week`)
                      `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds`
                AND `s 171ZZ6(2)(e) the person has been in the employment from the end of the relevant week to the day the child dies`
                      (facts's `the employment`)
                      (`s 171ZZ6(5) the last day of the relevant week` dies)
                      dies)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who satisfies the conditions in subsection (2) is entitled" (a failed paragraph (b), (c), (d) or (e); reading (a))
        ELSE `s 171ZZ6(2)(a) the person is a bereaved parent`
                 facts
                 `s 173(a) the person is under 18`

-- (2)(a) "that the person is a bereaved parent": see (3).
-- src:4021 | (a) that the person is a bereaved parent,
@ref s 171ZZ6(2)(a) (src:4021)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 171ZZ6(2) the person's case`
      `s 173(a) the person is under 18` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ6(2)(a) the person is a bereaved parent` MEANS
    `s 171ZZ6(3) the employee is a bereaved parent`
        (facts's `the child who died`)
        `s 173(a) the person is under 18`
        (facts's `the person satisfies the prescribed conditions as to relationship with the child who died`)

-- (2)(b) "a continuous period of at least 26 weeks ending with the relevant week".
-- src:4022 | (b) that the person has been in employed earner's employment with an employer for a continuous period of at least 26 weeks ending with the relevant week,
@ref s 171ZZ6(2)(b) (src:4022)
GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ6(2)(b) the person has been in employment for at least 26 weeks` MEANS
    weeks AT LEAST 26

-- (2)(c) "at the end of the relevant week the person was entitled to be in that employment (but see subsection (7))".
-- Where (7) omits the paragraph, the paragraph is taken as satisfied.
-- src:4023 | (c) that at the end of the relevant week the person was entitled to be in that employment (but see subsection (7)),
@ref s 171ZZ6(2)(c) (src:4023)
GIVEN `the person was entitled to be in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the paragraph is omitted by subsection (7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ6(2)(c) the person was entitled to be in that employment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the paragraph is omitted by subsection (7)`
    WHEN JUST omitted THEN omitted OR `the person was entitled to be in that employment`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the person was entitled to be in that employment`

-- (2)(d) "normal weekly earnings for the period of 8 weeks ending with the relevant week are not less than
-- the lower earnings limit in force under section 5(1)(a) at the end of the relevant week".
-- src:4024 | (d) that the person's normal weekly earnings for the period of 8 weeks ending with the relevant week are not less than the lower earnings limit in force under section 5(1)(a) at the end of the relevant week, and
@ref s 171ZZ6(2)(d) (src:4024)
GIVEN `normal weekly earnings in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ6(2)(d) the normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit` MEANS
    `normal weekly earnings in pounds` AT LEAST `s 5(1)(a) the lower earnings limit in force at the time in pounds`

-- (2)(e) "the person has been in employed earner's employment with the employer ... for a continuous period
-- beginning with the end of the relevant week and ending with the day on which the child dies".
-- The employment must have begun by the end of the relevant week and not have ended before the day of death.
-- src:4025 | (e) that the person has been in employed earner's employment with the employer by reference to whom the condition in paragraph (b) is satisfied for a continuous period beginning with the end of the relevant week and ending with the day on which the child dies.
@ref s 171ZZ6(2)(e) (src:4025)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the end of the relevant week` IS A DATE
      `the day the child dies` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ6(2)(e) the person has been in the employment from the end of the relevant week to the day the child dies` MEANS
        employment's `the employment began on` AT MOST `the end of the relevant week`
    AND CONSIDER employment's `the employment ended on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST ended THEN ended AT LEAST `the day the child dies`

-- (3) "an employee is a 'bereaved parent' if the employee satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with
-- a child who has died".  The child must be a "child" in this Part's sense (s 171ZZ14(1), s 171ZZ15).
-- (4) says the prescribed conditions may be framed by reference to care: a power, nothing to encode.
-- src:4026 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2) an employee is a “bereaved parent” if the employee satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with a child who has died.
@ref s 171ZZ6(3) (src:4026)
GIVEN child IS A `s 171ZZ6 the child who died`
      `s 173(a) the person is under 18` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the employee satisfies the prescribed conditions as to relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ6(3) the employee is a bereaved parent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 171ZZ14(1) the person who died was a child`
                 (child's `born dead`)
                 (child's `weeks of pregnancy when labour began`)
                 `s 173(a) the person is under 18`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): whether the dead child is a "child" is not covered (s 171ZZ14(1), s 171ZZ15(a))
    WHEN JUST isChild THEN
        IF isChild AND `the employee satisfies the prescribed conditions as to relationship`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an employee is a “bereaved parent” if the employee satisfies prescribed conditions as to relationship with a child who has died" (a failed "if"; reading (a))

-- (5) "'relevant week' means the week immediately before the one in which the child dies".
-- "Week" in this Part is a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday unless regulations prescribe another period (s 171ZZ14(5)).
-- src:4028 | (5) In subsection (2) “relevant week” means the week immediately before the one in which the child dies.
@ref s 171ZZ6(5) (src:4028)
GIVEN `the day the child dies` IS A DATE
      `regulations prescribe another period as the week in the person's case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Period
`s 171ZZ6(5) the relevant week` MEANS
    IF `regulations prescribe another period as the week in the person's case`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 171ZZ14(5) lets regulations prescribe "such other period" for the week
    ELSE JUST (Period WITH
                   `the first day` IS Date (Day `the day the child dies` MINUS (`Weekday of` `the day the child dies`) MINUS 7)
                   `the last day`  IS Date (Day `the day the child dies` MINUS (`Weekday of` `the day the child dies`) MINUS 1))

-- (5) again: the last day of the relevant week, on the Sunday-start convention (the end of the relevant week).
-- src:4028 | (5) In subsection (2) “relevant week” means the week immediately before the one in which the child dies.
@ref s 171ZZ6(5) (src:4028)
GIVEN `the day the child dies` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 171ZZ6(5) the last day of the relevant week` MEANS
    Date (Day `the day the child dies` MINUS (`Weekday of` `the day the child dies`) MINUS 1)

-- (6) "Where a person satisfies the conditions in subsection (2) as a result of the death of more than one
-- child, the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay in respect of each child."
-- The answers are one s 171ZZ6(1) answer per child who died.  NOTHING for any child makes the count NOTHING.
-- src:4029 | (6) Where a person satisfies the conditions in subsection (2) as a result of the death of more than one child, the person is entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay in respect of each child.
@ref s 171ZZ6(6) (src:4029)
GIVEN `the answers for each child who died` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 171ZZ6(6) the number of children in respect of whom the person is entitled` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN a YIELD isNothing a) `the answers for each child who died`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): at least one child's entitlement is not covered, so the count is not covered
    ELSE JUST (count (filter (GIVEN a YIELD a EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the answers for each child who died`))

-- (7) "In relation to a bereaved parent whose child dies before the day on which section 63(3) of the Welfare
-- Reform Act 2012 comes fully into force, subsection (2) above is to be read as if paragraph (c) were omitted."
-- That day is another Act's, so it is an input.  A death on or after that day is outside the limit.
-- src:4030 | (7) In relation to a bereaved parent whose child dies before the day on which section 63(3) of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 comes fully into force, subsection (2) above is to be read as if paragraph (c) were omitted.
@ref s 171ZZ6(7) (src:4030)
GIVEN `the day the child dies` IS A DATE
      `WRA 2012 s 63(3) the day on which it comes fully into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ6(7) paragraph (c) of subsection (2) is omitted` MEANS
    IF `the day the child dies` LESS THAN `WRA 2012 s 63(3) the day on which it comes fully into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the omission is for a child who "dies before the day"; a later death is for (2)(c) itself

§§ `s 171ZZ7 Entitlement: supplementary`

-- (1) "A person is entitled to payments ... in respect of any period only if the person gives notice to whoever
-- is liable to make the payments stating the week or weeks in respect of which they are to be made."
-- Given the notice, the entitlement is whatever s 171ZZ6(1) says; without it the text says no.
-- src:4032 | (1) A person is entitled to payments of statutory parental bereavement pay in respect of any period only if the person gives notice to whoever is liable to make the payments stating the week or weeks in respect of which they are to be made.
@ref s 171ZZ7(1) (src:4032)
GIVEN `the person is entitled under s 171ZZ6(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has given notice to whoever is liable, stating the weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ7(1) the person is entitled to payments for the weeks` MEANS
    IF `the person has given notice to whoever is liable, stating the weeks`
    THEN `the person is entitled under s 171ZZ6(1)`
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is entitled to payments of statutory parental bereavement pay in respect of any period only if the person gives notice"

-- (3) "The notice must be in writing if the person who is liable to pay ... so requests."
-- src:4034 | (3) The notice must be in writing if the person who is liable to pay the statutory parental bereavement pay so requests.
@ref s 171ZZ7(3) (src:4034)
GIVEN `the person who is liable to pay has asked for the notice to be in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ7(3) the notice satisfies the requirement as to writing` MEANS
    IF `the person who is liable to pay has asked for the notice to be in writing` AND (NOT `the notice is in writing`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must be in writing if the person who is liable to pay the statutory parental bereavement pay so requests."
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 171ZZ8 Liability to make payments`

-- (1) "The liability to make payments ... is a liability of any person of whom the person entitled to the payments
-- has been an employee as mentioned in subsection (2)(b) and (e) of that section."
-- The list of persons is not closed: subsection (3) lets regulations make the Commissioners liable instead.
-- src:4050 | (1) The liability to make payments of statutory parental bereavement pay under section 171ZZ6 is a liability of any person of whom the person entitled to the payments has been an employee as mentioned in subsection (2)(b) and (e) of that section.
@ref s 171ZZ8(1) (src:4050)
GIVEN `the person entitled has been an employee of this person as mentioned in s 171ZZ6(2)(b) and (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ8(1) the person is liable to make payments of statutory parental bereavement pay` MEANS
    IF `the person entitled has been an employee of this person as mentioned in s 171ZZ6(2)(b) and (e)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the liability is "a liability of any person of whom" the entitled person has been an employee; s 171ZZ8(3) lets regulations make the Commissioners liable

-- The same duty as a regulative rule.  The text gives no time limit and no consequence of default, so none is invented.
DECLARE `s 171ZZ8 Party` IS ONE OF
    `s 171ZZ8 the person liable to make the payments`

DECLARE `s 171ZZ8 Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 171ZZ8 makes a payment of statutory parental bereavement pay` HAS amount IS A NUMBER

-- src:4050 | (1) The liability to make payments of statutory parental bereavement pay under section 171ZZ6 is a liability of any person of whom the person entitled to the payments has been an employee as mentioned in subsection (2)(b) and (e) of that section.
@ref s 171ZZ8(1) (src:4050)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 171ZZ8 Party` `s 171ZZ8 Action`
`s 171ZZ8(1) the duty to make the payments` MEANS
    PARTY `s 171ZZ8 the person liable to make the payments`
    MUST `s 171ZZ8 makes a payment of statutory parental bereavement pay` amount
    HENCE FULFILLED

§§ `s 171ZZ9 Rate and period of pay`

-- (1) "payable at such fixed or earnings-related weekly rate as may be prescribed by regulations".  The Act gives no figure.
-- src:4054 | (1) Statutory parental bereavement pay is payable at such fixed or earnings-related weekly rate as may be prescribed by regulations, which may prescribe different kinds of rate for different cases.
@ref s 171ZZ9(1) (src:4054)
GIVEN `the weekly rate prescribed by regulations for the person's case, in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 171ZZ9(1) the weekly rate of statutory parental bereavement pay in pounds` MEANS
    `the weekly rate prescribed by regulations for the person's case, in pounds`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when the prescribed rate is not given

-- (2) "payable in respect of (a) such week within the qualifying period, or (b) such number of weeks, not exceeding the
-- prescribed number of weeks, within the qualifying period, as the person entitled may choose".
-- One week is a choice of one week.  A choice outside the limit (more weeks than the prescribed number, or weeks outside
-- the qualifying period) is outside the grant: the text does not say it is unpayable.
-- src:4055 | (2) Statutory parental bereavement pay is payable in respect of—
-- src:4056 | (a) such week within the qualifying period, or
-- src:4057 | (b) such number of weeks, not exceeding the prescribed number of weeks, within the qualifying period,
-- src:4058 | as the person entitled may choose in accordance with regulations.
@ref s 171ZZ9(2) (src:4055-4058)
GIVEN `the weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks chosen` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed number of weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `all the weeks chosen are within the qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 171ZZ9(2) the pay payable for the weeks chosen in pounds` MEANS
    IF `all the weeks chosen are within the qualifying period` AND `the number of weeks chosen` AT MOST `the prescribed number of weeks`
    THEN JUST (`the weekly rate in pounds` TIMES `the number of weeks chosen`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant covers weeks "within the qualifying period" and a number "not exceeding the prescribed number of weeks"

-- (3) "Provision under subsection (2)(b) must secure that the prescribed number of weeks is not less than two."
-- src:4059 | (3) Provision under subsection (2)(b) must secure that the prescribed number of weeks is not less than two.
@ref s 171ZZ9(3) (src:4059)
GIVEN `the prescribed number of weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ9(3) the prescribed number of weeks is allowed` MEANS
    IF `the prescribed number of weeks` AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must secure that the prescribed number of weeks is not less than two"

-- (5) "the qualifying period is to be determined in accordance with regulations, which must secure that it is a period
-- of at least 56 days beginning with the date of the child's death."  Both ends are counted.
-- src:4061 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (2), the qualifying period is to be determined in accordance with regulations, which must secure that it is a period of at least 56 days beginning with the date of the child's death.
@ref s 171ZZ9(5) (src:4061)
GIVEN qperiod IS A Period
      `the day the child dies` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ9(5) the qualifying period is allowed` MEANS
    IF     qperiod's `the first day` EQUALS `the day the child dies`
       AND (Day (qperiod's `the last day`) MINUS Day (qperiod's `the first day`)) PLUS 1 AT LEAST 56
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which must secure that it is a period of at least 56 days beginning with the date of the child's death"

-- (6) "A person is not liable to pay statutory parental bereavement pay to another in respect of any statutory pay week
-- during any part of which the other works under a contract of service with the person."
-- src:4062 | (6) A person is not liable to pay statutory parental bereavement pay to another in respect of any statutory pay week during any part of which the other works under a contract of service with the person.
@ref s 171ZZ9(6) (src:4062)
GIVEN `the other works under a contract of service with the person during any part of the statutory pay week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ9(6) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week` MEANS
    IF `the other works under a contract of service with the person during any part of the statutory pay week`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not liable to pay statutory parental bereavement pay to another in respect of any statutory pay week during any part of which the other works under a contract of service with the person."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): liability for a week the other does not work is for s 171ZZ8, not this subsection

-- (7) "It is immaterial for the purposes of subsection (6) whether the work referred to in that subsection is work under a
-- contract of service which existed immediately before the statutory pay week or ... which did not so exist."
-- So the answer is the (6) answer whichever way the second fact falls.
-- src:4063 | (7) It is immaterial for the purposes of subsection (6) whether the work referred to in that subsection is work under a contract of service which existed immediately before the statutory pay week or a contract of service which did not so exist.
@ref s 171ZZ9(7) (src:4063)
GIVEN `the other works under a contract of service with the person during any part of the statutory pay week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract of service existed immediately before the statutory pay week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ9(7) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week whether or not the contract existed before` MEANS
    `s 171ZZ9(6) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week`
        `the other works under a contract of service with the person during any part of the statutory pay week`

-- (8) "Except in such cases as may be prescribed, statutory parental bereavement pay is not payable to a person in respect
-- of a statutory pay week during any part of which the person works for any employer who is not liable to pay the person".
-- src:4064 | (8) Except in such cases as may be prescribed, statutory parental bereavement pay is not payable to a person in respect of a statutory pay week during any part of which the person works for any employer who is not liable to pay the person statutory parental bereavement pay.
@ref s 171ZZ9(8) (src:4064)
GIVEN `the person works during any part of the statutory pay week for an employer who is not liable to pay the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is one prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ9(8) the pay is payable for the statutory pay week` MEANS
    IF `the case is one prescribed by regulations`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except in such cases as may be prescribed"
    ELSE IF `the person works during any part of the statutory pay week for an employer who is not liable to pay the person`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "statutory parental bereavement pay is not payable to a person in respect of a statutory pay week during any part of which the person works for any employer who is not liable to pay the person"
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a week without that work is for the grant in subsection (2)

-- (10) "the amount payable ... for any day is to be taken as one seventh of the weekly rate."
-- src:4066 | (10) Where for any purpose of this Part or of regulations it is necessary to calculate the daily rate of statutory parental bereavement pay, the amount payable by way of statutory parental bereavement pay for any day is to be taken as one seventh of the weekly rate.
@ref s 171ZZ9(10) (src:4066)
GIVEN `the weekly rate in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZZ9(10) the daily rate in pounds` MEANS
    `the weekly rate in pounds` DIVIDED BY 7

-- (11) "'statutory pay week' ... means a week chosen by the person as a week in respect of which
-- statutory parental bereavement pay is to be payable; 'week' means any period of seven days."  The week convention is the core's
-- `any period of 7 days`.  Both ends of the period are counted.
-- src:4067 | (11) In this section—
-- src:4068 | “statutory pay week”, in relation to a person entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay, means a week chosen by the person as a week in respect of which statutory parental bereavement pay is to be payable;
-- src:4069 | “week” means any period of seven days.
@ref s 171ZZ9(11) (src:4067-4069)
GIVEN period IS A Period
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ9(11) the period is a week` MEANS
    (Day (period's `the last day`) MINUS Day (period's `the first day`)) PLUS 1 EQUALS 7

-- src:4067 | (11) In this section—
-- src:4068 | “statutory pay week”, in relation to a person entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay, means a week chosen by the person as a week in respect of which statutory parental bereavement pay is to be payable;
-- src:4069 | “week” means any period of seven days.
@ref s 171ZZ9(11) (src:4067-4069)
GIVEN period IS A Period
      `the person chose the week as a week in respect of which the pay is to be payable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ9(11) the period is a statutory pay week` MEANS
    `the person chose the week as a week in respect of which the pay is to be payable` AND `s 171ZZ9(11) the period is a week` period

-- src:4067 | (11) In this section—
-- src:4068 | “statutory pay week”, in relation to a person entitled to statutory parental bereavement pay, means a week chosen by the person as a week in respect of which statutory parental bereavement pay is to be payable;
-- src:4069 | “week” means any period of seven days.
@ref s 171ZZ9(11) (src:4067-4069)
`s 171ZZ9(11) the week convention` MEANS `any period of 7 days`

§§ `s 171ZZ10 Restrictions on contracting out`

-- (1) "An agreement is void to the extent that it purports (a) to exclude, limit or otherwise modify any provision of
-- this Part, or (b) to require a person to contribute ... towards any costs incurred by that person's employer or former
-- employer under this Part."  An agreement that purports neither is not said to be void here.
-- src:4071 | (1) An agreement is void to the extent that it purports—
-- src:4072 | (a) to exclude, limit or otherwise modify any provision of this Part, or
-- src:4073 | (b) to require a person to contribute (whether directly or indirectly) towards any costs incurred by that person's employer or former employer under this Part.
@ref s 171ZZ10(1) (src:4071-4073)
GIVEN `the agreement purports to exclude, limit or otherwise modify a provision of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement purports to require a person to contribute towards costs incurred by the person's employer or former employer under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ10(1) the agreement is void to that extent` MEANS
    IF `the agreement purports to exclude, limit or otherwise modify a provision of this Part`
       OR `the agreement purports to require a person to contribute towards costs incurred by the person's employer or former employer under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "void to the extent that it purports" (a) or (b); an agreement that purports neither is not covered by this subsection

-- (2) "An agreement between an employer and an employee, authorising any deductions from
-- statutory parental bereavement pay ..., is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a) if the employer (a) is authorised by that or another agreement to make
-- the same deductions from any contractual remuneration ..., or (b) would be so authorised if the employer were liable to
-- pay contractual remuneration in respect of that period."  A failed "if" is counted as the text's no (reading (a)).
-- src:4074 | (2) An agreement between an employer and an employee, authorising any deductions from statutory parental bereavement pay which the employer is liable to pay to the employee in respect of any period, is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a) if the employer—
-- src:4075 | (a) is authorised by that or another agreement to make the same deductions from any contractual remuneration which the employer is liable to pay in respect of the same period, or
-- src:4076 | (b) would be so authorised if the employer were liable to pay contractual remuneration in respect of that period.
@ref s 171ZZ10(2) (src:4074-4076)
GIVEN `the employer is authorised to make the same deductions from contractual remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer would be so authorised if liable to pay contractual remuneration for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ10(2) the agreement authorising deductions is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the employer is authorised to make the same deductions from contractual remuneration`
       OR `the employer would be so authorised if liable to pay contractual remuneration for the period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a) if the employer" is authorised, or would be (a failed "if"; reading (a))

§§ `s 171ZZ11 Relationship with contractual remuneration`

-- (1) "Subject to subsections (2) and (3), any entitlement to statutory parental bereavement pay does not affect any right
-- of a person in relation to remuneration under any contract of service ('contractual remuneration')."
-- Subsection (3) lets regulations decide which payments are contractual remuneration, so if they say otherwise the text alone cannot answer.
-- src:4078 | (1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), any entitlement to statutory parental bereavement pay does not affect any right of a person in relation to remuneration under any contract of service (“contractual remuneration”).
@ref s 171ZZ11(1) (src:4078)
GIVEN `regulations under subsection (3) treat the payment otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ11(1) the entitlement affects the person's right to contractual remuneration` MEANS
    IF `regulations under subsection (3) treat the payment otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (3) lets regulations say which payments are, and which are not, contractual remuneration
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any entitlement to statutory parental bereavement pay does not affect any right of a person in relation to remuneration under any contract of service"

-- (2)(a) "any contractual remuneration paid to a person by an employer ... in respect of any period is to go towards
-- discharging any liability of that employer to pay statutory parental bereavement pay to that person in respect of that period".
-- The remuneration paid is net of anything regulations treat as not being contractual remuneration (subsection (3)).
-- src:4080 | (a) any contractual remuneration paid to a person by an employer of that person in respect of any period is to go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay statutory parental bereavement pay to that person in respect of that period; and
@ref s 171ZZ11(2)(a) (src:4080)
GIVEN `liability to pay statutory parental bereavement pay for the period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `contractual remuneration paid for the same period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZZ11(2)(a) the liability to pay statutory parental bereavement pay that remains` MEANS
    IF `contractual remuneration paid for the same period, in pounds` AT LEAST `liability to pay statutory parental bereavement pay for the period, in pounds`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `liability to pay statutory parental bereavement pay for the period, in pounds` MINUS `contractual remuneration paid for the same period, in pounds`

-- (2)(b) "any statutory parental bereavement pay paid by an employer to a person who is an employee of that employer in
-- respect of any period is to go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay contractual remuneration".
-- src:4081 | (b) any statutory parental bereavement pay paid by an employer to a person who is an employee of that employer in respect of any period is to go towards discharging any liability of that employer to pay contractual remuneration to that person in respect of that period.
@ref s 171ZZ11(2)(b) (src:4081)
GIVEN `liability to pay contractual remuneration for the period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `statutory parental bereavement pay paid for the same period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 171ZZ11(2)(b) the liability to pay contractual remuneration that remains` MEANS
    IF `statutory parental bereavement pay paid for the same period, in pounds` AT LEAST `liability to pay contractual remuneration for the period, in pounds`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `liability to pay contractual remuneration for the period, in pounds` MINUS `statutory parental bereavement pay paid for the same period, in pounds`

§§ `s 171ZZ12 Crown employment`

-- "The provisions of this Part apply in relation to persons employed by or under the Crown as they apply in relation to
-- persons employed otherwise than by or under the Crown."  The answer is the same whoever the employer is.
-- src:4084 | The provisions of this Part apply in relation to persons employed by or under the Crown as they apply in relation to persons employed otherwise than by or under the Crown.
@ref s 171ZZ12 (src:4084)
GIVEN `the kind of employer` IS A `Kind of employer`
      `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ12 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of employer`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown`
    WHEN `a company or other body corporate` THEN `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown`
    WHEN `a government department, public authority or other body of persons` THEN `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown`
    WHEN `the Crown` THEN `the provisions of this Part apply to the person if the employer were not the Crown`

§§ `s 171ZZ13 Special classes of person`

-- (1) "The Secretary of State may with the concurrence of the Treasury make regulations modifying any provision of this Part
-- ... in its application to any person who is, has been or is to be (a) employed on board any ship, vessel, hovercraft or
-- aircraft; (b) outside Great Britain at any prescribed time or in any prescribed circumstances; or (c) in prescribed
-- employment in connection with continental shelf operations, as defined in section 120(2)."
-- This is what the power reaches; the regulations themselves are outside the sources (subsection (2) lists what they may do).
-- src:4086 | (1) The Secretary of State may with the concurrence of the Treasury make regulations modifying any provision of this Part in such manner as the Secretary of State thinks proper in its application to any person who is, has been or is to be—
-- src:4087 | (a) employed on board any ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft;
-- src:4088 | (b) outside Great Britain at any prescribed time or in any prescribed circumstances; or
-- src:4089 | (c) in prescribed employment in connection with continental shelf operations, as defined in section 120(2).
@ref s 171ZZ13(1) (src:4086-4089)
GIVEN `the person is employed on board a ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is outside Great Britain at a prescribed time or in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in prescribed employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ13(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` MEANS
    IF     `the person is employed on board a ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft`
        OR `the person is outside Great Britain at a prescribed time or in prescribed circumstances`
        OR (`the person is in prescribed employment` AND `s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for a person who is, has been or is to be in one of the three classes

§§ `s 171ZZ14 Supplementary`

-- Nouns for the kinds of change that "modifications" names.
DECLARE `s 171ZZ14(1) kind of change` IS ONE OF
    `s 171ZZ14(1) an addition`
    `s 171ZZ14(1) an omission`
    `s 171ZZ14(1) an amendment`
    `s 171ZZ14(1) another kind of change`

-- (1) "'child' means a person under the age of 18 (see also section 171ZZ15 ...)".
-- A child born alive is a child if under 18 (s 173(a), asked as an input).  A child stillborn is a child through s 171ZZ15(a).
-- src:4097 | “child” means a person under the age of 18 (see also section 171ZZ15 for the application of this Part in relation to stillbirths);
@ref s 171ZZ14(1) (src:4097)
GIVEN `born dead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `weeks of pregnancy when labour began` IS A NUMBER
      `s 173(a) the person is under 18` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ14(1) the person who died was a child` MEANS
    IF `born dead`
    THEN `s 171ZZ15(a) the child stillborn after twenty-four weeks of pregnancy is a child` `born dead` `weeks of pregnancy when labour began`
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 173(a) the person is under 18`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 173(a) does not answer for this age
         WHEN JUST under18 THEN
             IF under18 THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“child” means a person under the age of 18"

-- (1) "'employer', in relation to a person who is an employee, means a person who (first limb) under section 6 is liable to
-- pay secondary Class 1 contributions in relation to any of the earnings of the person who is an employee, or (second limb)
-- would be liable to pay such contributions but for (A) the condition in section 6(1)(b), or (B) the employee being under
-- the age of 16."  The limb labels are not in the converter text; "first limb", "second limb", "(A)" and "(B)" are mine.
-- src:4098 | “employer”, in relation to a person who is an employee, means a person who—
-- src:4099 | under section 6 is liable to pay secondary Class 1 contributions in relation to any of the earnings of the person who is an employee, or
-- src:4100 | would be liable to pay such contributions but for—
-- src:4101 | the condition in section 6(1)(b), or
-- src:4102 | the employee being under the age of 16;
@ref s 171ZZ14(1) (src:4098-4102)
GIVEN `s 6 the person is liable to pay secondary Class 1 contributions in relation to earnings of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 6 the person would be liable but for the condition in section 6(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 6 the person would be liable but for the employee being under 16` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 173(a) the person is under 16` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ14(1) the person is the employer of the employee` MEANS
    IF     `s 6 the person is liable to pay secondary Class 1 contributions in relation to earnings of the employee`
        OR `s 6 the person would be liable but for the condition in section 6(1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF NOT `s 6 the person would be liable but for the employee being under 16`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employer”, in relation to a person who is an employee, means a person who" is liable, or would be but for the condition or the age
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 173(a) the person is under 16`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): s 173(a) does not answer whether the employee is under 16
              WHEN JUST under16 THEN
                  IF under16 THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a person who" would be liable "but for ... the employee being under the age of 16"; the employee is not under 16

-- (1) "'modifications' includes additions, omissions and amendments, and related expressions are to be read accordingly".
-- src:4103 | “modifications” includes additions, omissions and amendments, and related expressions are to be read accordingly;
@ref s 171ZZ14(1) (src:4103)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 171ZZ14(1) kind of change`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ14(1) the change is a modification` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 171ZZ14(1) an addition` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 171ZZ14(1) an omission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 171ZZ14(1) an amendment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 171ZZ14(1) another kind of change` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes additions, omissions and amendments" does not close the list

-- (1) "'prescribed' means prescribed by regulations".
-- src:4104 | “prescribed” means prescribed by regulations.
@ref s 171ZZ14(1) (src:4104)
GIVEN `the matter is prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ14(1) the matter is prescribed` MEANS
    IF `the matter is prescribed by regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“prescribed” means prescribed by regulations"

-- (2) "In this Part, 'employee' means a person who is gainfully employed in Great Britain either under a contract of
-- service or in an office (including elective office) with earnings (within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5)."
-- "Gainfully" is read as adding nothing to "with earnings" (fork in NOTES).  Whether the person has "earnings" in that
-- sense is a borrowed fact.  Whether adjacent waters count as Great Britain (s 172(a)) is already in the core's field.
-- src:4105 | (2) In this Part, “employee” means a person who is gainfully employed in Great Britain either under a contract of service or in an office (including elective office) with earnings (within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5).
@ref s 171ZZ14(2) (src:4105)
GIVEN employment IS AN Employment
      `the person has earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ14(2) the person is an employee` MEANS
    IF     employment's `carried on in Great Britain`
       AND (employment's `held under a contract of service` OR employment's `held in an office`)
       AND `the person has earnings within the meaning of Parts 1 to 5`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employee” means a person who is gainfully employed in Great Britain either under a contract of service or in an office (including elective office) with earnings"

-- (5) "In this Part, except section 171ZZ9, 'week' means a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or such other period as
-- may be prescribed in relation to any particular case or class of cases."  The core's fifth week convention.
-- src:4112 | (5) In this Part, except section 171ZZ9, “week” means a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or such other period as may be prescribed in relation to any particular case or class of cases.
@ref s 171ZZ14(5) (src:4112)
`s 171ZZ14(5) the week convention` MEANS `a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or another prescribed period`

-- src:4112 | (5) In this Part, except section 171ZZ9, “week” means a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or such other period as may be prescribed in relation to any particular case or class of cases.
@ref s 171ZZ14(5) (src:4112)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `regulations prescribe another period as the week in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 171ZZ14(5) the first day of the week containing the day` MEANS
    IF `regulations prescribe another period as the week in the case`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such other period as may be prescribed"
    ELSE JUST (Date (Day day MINUS (`Weekday of` day)))

-- (6) "a person's normal weekly earnings are, subject to subsection (8), to be taken to be the average weekly earnings which
-- in the relevant period have been paid to the person or paid for the person's benefit under the contract of service with
-- the employer in question."  (7): "earnings" and "relevant period" are whatever regulations say, so the total and the
-- number of weeks are inputs.  (8): in prescribed cases regulations calculate it, so the text alone cannot answer.
-- src:4113 | (6) For the purposes of this Part, a person's normal weekly earnings are, subject to subsection (8), to be taken to be the average weekly earnings which in the relevant period have been paid to the person or paid for the person's benefit under the contract of service with the employer in question.
-- src:4114 | (7) For the purposes of subsection (6), “earnings” and “relevant period” have the meanings given to them by regulations.
-- src:4115 | (8) In such cases as may be prescribed, a person's normal weekly earnings are to be calculated in accordance with regulations.
@ref s 171ZZ14(6) (src:4113-4115)
GIVEN `the earnings paid in the relevant period, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks in the relevant period` IS A NUMBER
      `regulations prescribe another calculation in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 171ZZ14(6) the person's normal weekly earnings in pounds` MEANS
    IF `regulations prescribe another calculation in the case`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (8), "In such cases as may be prescribed"
    ELSE IF `the number of weeks in the relevant period` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN JUST (`the earnings paid in the relevant period, in pounds` DIVIDED BY `the number of weeks in the relevant period`)
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an average over a relevant period with no weeks is not defined

§§ `s 171ZZ15 Application in relation to stillbirths`

-- (a) "references to a child include a child stillborn after twenty-four weeks of pregnancy".
-- "Include" adds and does not close, so a child stillborn at 24 weeks or fewer is not covered.  "After 24 weeks" is read as
-- more than 24 weeks have passed (fork in NOTES); the weeks may carry a fraction (24 weeks and 1 day is 24 and 1/7).
-- src:4128 | (a) references to a child include a child stillborn after twenty-four weeks of pregnancy, and
@ref s 171ZZ15(a) (src:4128)
GIVEN `born dead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `weeks of pregnancy when labour began` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 171ZZ15(a) the child stillborn after twenty-four weeks of pregnancy is a child` MEANS
    IF `born dead` AND `weeks of pregnancy when labour began` GREATER THAN `the weeks of pregnancy named in the stillbirth rule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include a child stillborn after twenty-four weeks of pregnancy" adds a case and does not close the list

-- (b) "references to the death of a child are to be read, in relation to a stillborn child, as references to the birth of the child".
-- src:4129 | (b) references to the death of a child are to be read, in relation to a stillborn child, as references to the birth of the child.
@ref s 171ZZ15(b) (src:4129)
GIVEN `born dead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the child was born` IS A DATE
      `the day the child died` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 171ZZ15(b) the day taken as the day the child dies` MEANS
    IF `born dead`
    THEN JUST `the day the child was born`
    ELSE `the day the child died`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent) when no day of death is given
